1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:05,000
Today we turn a simple floor plan and a few photos into a 3D model of a flat.

2
00:00:05,050 --> 00:00:09,740
Then we furnish it, and try out new ideas, like a round dining table in the kitchen.

3
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:11,766
No CAD knowledge needed.

4
00:00:11,816 --> 00:00:15,370
You just say what you want, and an AI agent does the modeling.

5
00:00:18,450 --> 00:00:23,840
We use SOMA, a free and open-source app where an AI coding agent builds 3D models for you.

6
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:25,220
Get it at somacad.app.

7
00:00:27,170 --> 00:00:28,900
We start with a new, empty model.

8
00:00:30,137 --> 00:00:31,828
Import brings in our material:

9
00:00:31,878 --> 00:00:35,194
a sketch of the floor plan, and a few photos of each room.

10
00:00:35,244 --> 00:00:39,307
SOMA copies them into the model folder, where the agent can find them.

11
00:00:40,007 --> 00:00:41,030
The sketch is simple:

12
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:43,944
the rooms, the doors and windows, and a few measurements.

13
00:00:43,994 --> 00:00:47,009
Just like you would draw your own flat with a tape measure.

14
00:00:48,237 --> 00:00:52,464
The photos show a historic flat in Heidelberg that is now a small museum.

15
00:00:52,514 --> 00:00:54,447
We drew the sketch to match them.

16
00:00:56,770 --> 00:00:58,334
Next, we start the agent.

17
00:00:58,384 --> 00:01:01,950
Click the plus above the terminal, and pick Claude Code.

18
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,260
Other command line agents work too.

19
00:01:06,010 --> 00:01:07,429
First, the flat itself.

20
00:01:07,479 --> 00:01:10,112
We just tell the agent which file to read:

21
00:01:10,162 --> 00:01:13,740
floor, walls, doors and windows, as drawn in the sketch.

22
00:01:15,127 --> 00:01:19,467
The agent reads the sketch, writes the model as code, builds it, and checks the result.

23
00:01:19,517 --> 00:01:21,737
This takes a few minutes, so we speed it up.

24
00:01:22,804 --> 00:01:24,288
And here is our flat in 3D:

25
00:01:24,338 --> 00:01:27,406
every wall, door and window where the sketch has them.

26
00:01:29,771 --> 00:01:30,620
Now we furnish it.

27
00:01:30,670 --> 00:01:36,061
The agent should look at the photos, and add simple models of the furniture it sees, each in the right room.

28
00:01:37,454 --> 00:01:42,224
It goes through the photos room by room, and builds every piece from simple boxes and cylinders.

29
00:01:42,924 --> 00:01:48,254
When it is done, it tells you what it had to guess, like the size of the sofa, so you know what to check.

30
00:01:49,310 --> 00:01:50,699
And there it is, furnished.

31
00:01:50,749 --> 00:01:55,440
Every piece of furniture is a part of its own, sorted into groups in the structure tree.

32
00:01:56,643 --> 00:02:01,322
To look at it like a floor plan, view it from the top, and cut the walls with a section.

33
00:02:01,372 --> 00:02:03,253
Now you can see every room at once.

34
00:02:03,953 --> 00:02:12,151
From the photos, it picked up the red sofa and the sewing table, the old stove and the kitchen cabinet, the two beds with the wardrobe, and the bathtub.

35
00:02:13,901 --> 00:02:14,941
Now the fun part:

36
00:02:14,991 --> 00:02:16,031
trying out ideas.

37
00:02:16,081 --> 00:02:19,430
How would the kitchen look with a round dining table?

38
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:23,391
Click the table, send it to the agent, and say what you want.

39
00:02:24,091 --> 00:02:27,181
The agent replaces the table, and moves the chairs around it.

40
00:02:27,881 --> 00:02:30,039
Only the table and the chairs change.

41
00:02:30,089 --> 00:02:32,237
The rest of the flat stays as it is.

42
00:02:33,087 --> 00:02:37,297
And here is the kitchen with a round table, one meter across, and four chairs around it.

43
00:02:39,754 --> 00:02:44,288
We asked for an adjustable size, so the diameter shows up in the Parameters tab.

44
00:02:44,338 --> 00:02:47,383
Drag the slider, and SOMA rebuilds the flat by itself.

45
00:02:47,433 --> 00:02:49,324
The agent is not needed for this.

46
00:02:50,024 --> 00:02:52,620
Every change is saved as a version on the timeline.

47
00:02:52,670 --> 00:02:55,834
So you can try as many ideas as you like, and always go back.

48
00:02:57,184 --> 00:02:57,698
That's it:

49
00:02:57,748 --> 00:03:01,872
from a sketch and a few photos to a furnished flat in 3D, without any CAD.

50
00:03:01,922 --> 00:03:07,394
Get SOMA for free at somacad.app, bring the agent you already use, and try it with your own flat.
